# SHA-256 fingerprint of the Caribou app signing certificate
# (CN=Bisoncraft LLC, O=Bisoncraft LLC, C=US; RSA 4096; valid until 2056-11-17).
#
# This is the app's identity on a device: Android installs an update only when
# it is signed by the certificate of the installed copy. The directly
# distributed APK is signed with this key, and Google Play holds a copy and
# signs what it serves with it, so both channels carry this fingerprint.
# release/package-android.sh fails a build whose APK is signed by anything
# else. Check an APK against it with:
#
#     apksigner verify --print-certs caribou-<version>-android-arm64.apk
8C:D1:54:3F:3A:2F:35:9F:48:73:10:F8:0C:C9:BD:89:13:DC:23:03:FD:D0:50:3A:7F:7D:E2:E7:78:DD:02:7F
